note draft
# A glob-to-role mapping from the repository these bindings were AUTHORED in, not from this one. Measured
# 2026-08-30: it maps four `*.note` globs, and @term/bind holds ZERO `.note` files. `../book/**` does not exist
# here at all, and the three `../code/{javascript,browser,node}/**` directories that do exist hold 392, 1768 and
# 730 `.tree` files respectively, which this file does not mention.
#
# So there is nothing here to rewrite in the current `role.tree` spelling (`role host` / `take @/data/**`): the
# package declares no `role` in its deck.tree, builds clean at 3,091 files without one, and adding a role file
# could only change that for the worse. The `bind dock, loan js` half has no equivalent either, because a modern
# Term module picks its backend by the native path (`native/{platform}/...`) rather than by a glob mapping.
#
# Kept, not deleted, because it records how the binding library was laid out where it was generated, which is
# what package-builds-0013 is about. Nothing reads it. See note/term/project/package-builds.md.

load @term/mesh
  find mill code
  find mill book

file ../book/**/*.note
  bind role, loan book

file ../code/javascript/**/*.note
  bind role, loan code
  bind dock, loan js

file ../code/browser/**/*.note
  bind role, loan code
  bind dock, loan js

file ../code/node/**/*.note
  bind role, loan code
  bind dock, loan js
